   "text": "I read the drawing as an ezetimibe-type azetidin-2-one carrying a substituted biphenyl in place of the 4-hydroxyphenyl group.\n\n**Structure, region by region**\n- **Core:** a four-membered \u03b2-lactam ring with N, C=O, and two CH carbons.\n- **Nitrogen:** it carries a 4-fluorophenyl group.\n- **C4 (next to N):** it carries a 4-substituted phenyl ring, drawn with a wedge. That phenyl is joined to a second ring bearing a methyl, a hydroxyl and a methoxy. The methyl and methoxy sit meta to the biaryl bond, and the OH sits para to it, between them.\n- **C3 (next to C=O):** it carries an H drawn with a wedge, and a chain CH2\u2013CH2\u2013CH(OH)\u2013(4-fluorophenyl). The carbinol OH is also on a wedge.\n\n**Stereochemistry from the wedges**\n- **C4:** the CIP priority order is N > aryl > C3, and the lowest-priority H points away. N, aryl, C3 run counterclockwise on the page, so C4 is S.\n- **C3:** the priority order is C=O > C4 > CH2. These run counterclockwise on the page, but H points toward the viewer, so the true sense is clockwise and C3 is R.\n- **Carbinol carbon:** the priority order is OH > aryl > CH2. These run counterclockwise on the page, and H points away, so it is S.\n\nThis gives (3R,4S) in the ring and S at the carbinol, the same configuration as ezetimibe. I therefore started from the ezetimibe SMILES and replaced the 4-hydroxyphenyl group with the substituted biphenyl.\n\nSMILES: O[C@@H](CC[C@@H]1C(=O)N(c2ccc(F)cc2)[C@@H]1c1ccc(cc1)-c1cc(C)c(O)c(OC)c1)c1ccc(F)cc1"
